## Key Learning

Monitoring alerts should always be validated before assuming an infrastructure outage. In this incident, the ESXi hosts, VMware environment, 
and network were all operating normally, but inconsistent DNS resolution caused the monitoring platform to associate hostnames with incorrect IP 
addresses. Systematically comparing monitoring data, VMware inventory, and DNS responses helped isolate the issue to a configuration mismatch. 
This case highlights the importance of validating name resolution paths during infrastructure discovery and monitoring integration.
